==============================================================================
   HOW TO READ THIS
   D* is set on the CALIBRATION set and verified on the UNTOUCHED
   AUDIT set. If the audit rate is near 0.05 the detector is
   correctly sized against arbitrary smooth scalar responses AND
   against realistic anisotropy-mimicking defects -- which is a much
   stronger claim than Run AC's, where the null was an off-grid
   member of the detector's own grammar.
   The per-generator column says WHICH defect the detector confuses
   for anisotropy. A rate well above 0.05 in one row names a
   systematic that must be controlled before any tensor claim.

